[gd_scene load_steps=21 format=3]

; Four-furrow mounted mouldboard plough, 14-inch bodies on a Category 2 headstock. Authored in
; the LOWERED (working) pose with the origin ON THE LOWER PIN LINE — the frame HitchLinkage
; solves against — so the scene as it looks in the editor is the plough in the soil. Ground is
; at y = -0.21 in this frame (measured: the tractor's lower-link balls settle 0.21 m above the
; ground when fully lowered, 0.78 m when raised), so every share reaches 0.25 m under it, and
; the front share still clears the ground by ~0.4 m once the hitch lifts and tips the plough
; back.
;
; The beam is YAWED 22.7deg to the left of travel and the four bodies step out along it, one
; 14-inch furrow across and 0.85 m (the interbody clearance) apart — that asymmetry is not a
; modelling slip, it is what a conventional right-hand plough is: each body cuts the furrow the
; one ahead of it left behind. The depth wheel runs on the land side behind the last body.
; Shares and mouldboards are bright steel against the blue frame so the working edge reads
; from the chase camera. NO CollisionShape and no PTO gear: this machine is pulled, not driven
; (see plough.gd).

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://src/vehicles/tractor/implements/plough.gd" id="1_plough"]
[ext_resource type="PackedScene" path="res://src/vehicles/tractor/implements/headstock.tscn" id="2_head"]

